A||N||5||FieroJoe||Ignition Lock questions...||||1||
Z||000000||FieroJoe||04-24-2001||10:22 PM||||Im wonderin if it would be ok to lubricate my ignition lock with some graphite or Lock-eez.   I use Lock-eez on my exterior lock cylenders, but I didnt want to mess anything up with the ignition one.<P>The reason why I think this needs to be done is that sometimes the lock can be picky and wont turn on, even when I move the steering wheel around a little bit and when I'm using a key that's been used in it many times before.  It also will rarely go into ACC mode.  I have to really play around with it to get there.  It will maybe go in after about 20-30 tries, kinda annoying.<P>What about replacing the whole thing, to correct it all?  About what do they cost, and how hard to replace.  I have a 5spd tranny.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: FieroJoe87<BR>87 Coupe 5spd<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||operator64||04-24-2001||10:29 PM||||   Just replaced mine the other night at the local convencience store fuel pumps. At AutoZone it cost me about $12 for the ignition lock with keys and about 15 minutes to replace it. Special tools you will need is steering wheel puller, and a lock plate removing tool, with these and ordinary hand tools it should be a breeze.<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000002||theogre||04-24-2001||11:01 PM||||There is a link in my cave's steering column article that will get you all the pitures on how to do it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Songman||04-24-2001||11:19 PM||||One of my 88s will NOT go into ACC at all!<P>But lock cylinders are generally pretty easy as a rule. Never done a Fiero, but I have done others.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Haze_Performance||04-25-2001||01:42 AM||||Yep...I would just relpace it. Its very easy to do. Ive done a few Fieros & its a peice of cake.. good luck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Haze  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/haze8588logo.gif">    </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>Pennock's Fiero Forum Members Photo Page</A><P><A HREF="http://www.clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/ws6fiero" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero Club</A>||||reg||14
Z||000005||FieroJoe||04-25-2001||10:23 AM||||Thanks for the replies.  My dad has done a few before, but I showed him what was under the center cover of my steering wheel and he said he hasnt seen anything like it.  But, it sounds easy enough, I'll probably do it to save me the frustration of having to jiggle everything around to turn the key.  I'll definatly read that cave article.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: FieroJoe87<BR>87 Coupe 5spd<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
